(7514461, 1199738, 86447, '<td valign="top">I love this, Janine!  Congratulations on your HM!<br/></td>', 'I love this, Janine!  Congratulations on your HM!', '2017-05-18 14:51:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7514618, 1199738, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>Well done Janine, a great result for a great image, well deserved. What a great choice of subject for the challenge and very well executed too. Its inevitable that in this sort of difficult exposure you will get some blown highlights from the brightest parts but you have controlled it all well, the all-important interior is very well exposed. Lighthouses are fascinating structures and this is no exception a lovely building. I like Arts comment about the sign! So, what does it say?</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well Well done Janine, a great result for a great image, well deserved. What a great choice of subject for the challenge and very well executed too. Its inevitable that in this sort of difficult exposure you will get some blown highlights from the brightest parts but you have controlled it all well, the all-important interior is very well exposed. Lighthouses are fascinating structures and this is no exception a lovely building. I like Arts comment about the sign! So, what does it say?', '2017-05-19 06:06:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7514619, 1199599, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An image that does not meet the challenge<br/> <br/>In so far as it goes you do have focus from foreground to the hut so in that respect it partially meets the challenge Marcel but I dont think you have chosen the best subject for the challenge because this is not at all challenging in respect of a deep DOF. The emphasis for a successful entry must be on a DEEP DOF this choice of subject is in no way deep. The bland uninteresting sky actually serves a purpose in isolating the hut from the world around it so it is effective in creating a different look to your image but again this is not really the purpose of this challenge. A look at the front page will probably explain better than I am what was expected for the challenge and Im sure you will agree that your image differs significantly in this respect?</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An image that does not meet the challenge In so far as it goes you do have focus from foreground to the hut so in that respect it partially meets the challenge Marcel but I dont think you have chosen the best subject for the challenge because this is not at all challenging in respect of a deep DOF. The emphasis for a successful entry must be on a DEEP DOF this choice of subject is in no way deep. The bland uninteresting sky actually serves a purpose in isolating the hut from the world around it so it is effective in creating a different look to your image but again this is not really the purpose of this challenge. A look at the front page will probably explain better than I am what was expected for the challenge and Im sure you will agree that your image differs significantly in this respect?', '2017-05-19 06:24:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7514620, 1199164, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An image that does not meet the challenge<br/> <br/>Im sorry Oli but Im gonna have to fundamentally disagree with you on your unlimited dof definition. I do agree that the point of focus is all important to make best use of any chosen aperture  but the size of that aperture is also important in defining the zone of sharpness within your image. Your image does not have sharpness between the three lights there is clearly softness in the foreground lamp especially when compared with the furthest lamp which is not at all surprising given your f2.8 aperture, something nearer f11 may have given you the sharpness needed for this challenge.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An image that does not meet the challenge Im sorry Oli but Im gonna have to fundamentally disagree with you on your unlimited dof definition. I do agree that the point of focus is all important to make best use of any chosen aperture  but the size of that aperture is also important in defining the zone of sharpness within your image. Your image does not have sharpness between the three lights there is clearly softness in the foreground lamp especially when compared with the furthest lamp which is not at all surprising given your f2.8 aperture, something nearer f11 may have given you the sharpness needed for this challenge.', '2017-05-19 06:45:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7514674, 1199738, 96664, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=961063" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/95000-99999/96664/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_961063.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/95000-99999/96664/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_961063.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/95000-99999/96664/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_961063.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Been there! Haha! Great shot Janine! :)</td>', '  Been there! Haha! Great shot Janine! :)', '2017-05-19 10:22:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7514767, 1199604, 87278, '<td valign="top">Awesome!<br/></td>', 'Awesome!', '2017-05-20 09:03:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7514768, 1199741, 87278, '<td valign="top">Anything to do with railway - engine, car and track especially - fascinated me. Even without such predisposition this is a brilliant take.</td>', 'Anything to do with railway - engine, car and track especially - fascinated me. Even without such predisposition this is a brilliant take.', '2017-05-20 09:13:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7515418, 1199520, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>A very standard, hastily shot bee-on-a-flower macro and frankly not a very good one at that.  Bee appears to be out of focus and the flowers are blown out in areas...but as has already been said several times by the commenters, this photo does not meet the challenge criteria, and that is critical on this site. If you don''t make even the faintest attempt to try and make a deep DOF entry for a deep DOF challenge, then you''re wasting your time.  As you did not enter your camera''s settings, you leave me nothing to go on.  <br/> <br/>If you wish to truly improve your photography and chances of doing well here, please feel free to PM me...En Anglais svp, so I don''t have to resort to using a dreadful translation program!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! A very standard, hastily shot bee-on-a-flower macro and frankly not a very good one at that.  Bee appears to be out of focus and the flowers are blown out in areas...but as has already been said several times by the commenters, this photo does not meet the challenge criteria, and that is critical on this site. If you don''t make even the faintest attempt to try and make a deep DOF entry for a deep DOF challenge, then you''re wasting your time.  As you did not enter your camera''s settings, you leave me nothing to go on.   If you wish to truly improve your photography and chances of doing well here, please feel free to PM me...En Anglais svp, so I don''t have to resort to using a dreadful translation program!', '2017-05-24 21:58:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7515716, 1199555, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>A very good attempt at a deep DOF shot for the challenge, but there are many issues you need to address.  First off, you may want to study up on composition and pay attention to what you could have done to make the subject more interesting to look at.  I understand it''s berthed, but there are ways to shoot a magnificent ship like this and work with the setting around it.  Your ISO is reasonable for a mostly dark subject, but Nikon''s infamous noise, even at low ISOs, is evident here.  Also watch for the blown-out clouds, always a bugaboo when you''re shooting both black and white in the same shot.<br/> <br/>Hope this critique has been helpful, do some homework and I hope to see more of your entries soon.  Feel free to PM me with any comments or questions.  Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! A very good attempt at a deep DOF shot for the challenge, but there are many issues you need to address.  First off, you may want to study up on composition and pay attention to what you could have done to make the subject more interesting to look at.  I understand it''s berthed, but there are ways to shoot a magnificent ship like this and work with the setting around it.  Your ISO is reasonable for a mostly dark subject, but Nikon''s infamous noise, even at low ISOs, is evident here.  Also watch for the blown-out clouds, always a bugaboo when you''re shooting both black and white in the same shot. Hope this critique has been helpful, do some homework and I hope to see more of your entries soon.  Feel free to PM me with any comments or questions.  Susan', '2017-05-26 21:58:33.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
